    "data": {
      "text": "Vinod Rathod vs The Union Of India Thr. Its Secretary ... on 30 \nJanuary, 2024 \nAuthor: G. S. Kulkarni\nBench: G. S. Kulkarni\n 910-Wp-134\nS.R.Joshi\n In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay\n Appellate Side Civil Jurisdiction\n Writ Petition No. 1344 Of 2024\n Shri Vinod Rathod ... Petitio\n Versus\n The Union of India\n & Others ...Responde\n Mr. Harshwardhan Karande with Ms. Poonam Pal, for the Petitioner. \n Ms. Shehnaz V. Bharucha, for Respondent No.1- Uoi.\n Ms. Shruti D. Vyas, Addl. G.P. with Ms. P. N. Diwan, Agp for\n Respondent No.3.\n Adv. Sukanya Bhavnik, for Respondent No.2- Fssai. \n _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ __\n Coram: G. S. Kulkarni &\n Firdosh P. Pooniwalla, Jj. \n Dated: 30th January, 2024\n _______________________\n P.C. \nThis Petition raises an issue of serious concern with regard to the sale of biscuits which have already expired by affixing a false label on the package. These biscuits were purchased by the Petitioner from Respondent No.5. The biscuits are stated to be manufactured by Respondent No.4 \"ITC Sunfeast Biscuit\". The Petitioner, in fact, has contended that, by consuming some of these biscuits,\nthe Petitioner's daughter took unwell. The Petitioner has approached the Food & Safety Authorities and various other authorities. However, the authorities have not listened to the said complaints of the Petitioner. It is for this reason that the present Petition has been filed. \n2 The Union of India is represented by Ms. Bharucha, who has been served with a copy of the Petition. We have asked Ms. Bharucha to appear for Respondent No.1. Ms.Sukanya Bhaumik appears for the Food Safety and 30 January, 2024 910-WP-1344-2024.DOC Standard Authority of Vinod Rathod vs The Union Of India Thr. Its Secretary ... on 30 January, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/135103443/\n1 India. State of Maharashtra is represented by Ms. Vyas, learned Addl. G.P. and Ms. Diwan, learned AGP.\n3 Leave to amend to correct the cause title of the Petition in respect of the description of Respondent No.4.\n4 Issue notice to Respondent Nos.4 & 5, returnable after two weeks. In addition to the Court notice,\nthe learned Counsel for the Petitioner is permitted to serve Respondent Nos. 4 & 5 by all permissible modes including private service, and place on record affidavit of service. \n5 In the event, despite service of notice, Respondent Nos. 4 & 5 are not represented on the adjourned date of hearing, the Court shall proceed to hear the Petitioner and the other Respondents who appear and pass appropriate orders. \n6 Stand over to 14th February, 2024- HOB. \n(FIRDOSH P. POONIWALLA, J.) (G. S. KULKARNI , J.) 30 January, 2024 Vinod Rathod vs The Union Of India Thr. Its Secretary ... on 30 January, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/135103443/\n2",
      "preamble_end_char_offset": 747
    },
